The '''Dwuni''' were a [[species]] of short [[Limb|bipedal]] [[Sentience|sentients]]. They had large heads with sharp-[[tooth]]ed [[mouth]]s and [[eye]]s on stalks. Two Dwuni [[Gender|brothers]], [[Blawz]] and [[Crodit]], worked as [[Slavery|enslaved]] [[miner]]s in the [[Spice mines of Kessel|mines]] of the [[planet]] [[Kessel]] in [[10 BBY]]. Despite enjoying their work, they were among the liberated miners who poured out of the mines during a [[Raid on Kessel|revolt]] that [[Standard year|year]]. [[5 BBY|Five years]] later, three Dwuni were employed at a store in [[Ferrix City]] on the world [[Ferrix]], although they were scared out of the building by the [[human]] [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Pre-Mor Authority]] [[Deputy Inspector]] [[Syril Karn]] while he was preparing an [[Ambush on Ferrix|ambush]] on the [[thief]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]].

==Biology and appearance==
The Dwuni were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]],<ref name="SoloGuide" /> the members of which were generally half the height of an adult [[human]].<ref name="Reckoning" /><ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> [[Limb|Bipedal]], they had two hands with three [[claw]]ed digits each. A Dwuni's head was roughly one-quarter to one-third of its body size,<ref name="SoloGuide" /> and it had an elongated shape with a flattened top that gradually sloped down toward their face.<ref name="Reckoning" /> The latter featured a large, sharp-[[tooth]]ed [[mouth]] with a prominent chin; a slit-shaped [[nose]];<ref name="SoloGuide" /> and short eye-stalks with [[eye]]s that had large [[Color|black]] pupils. On the sides of their head the Dwuni had a pair of hearing orifices with no external [[ear]]s, and their skin could be tan<ref name="Reckoning" /> or orange in color.<ref name="SoloGuide" />

==Society and culture==
Members of the Dwuni society identified as belonging to at least one&mdash;male&mdash;[[gender]].<ref name="SoloGuide" />

==Dwuni in the galaxy==
[[File:BlawzAndCrodit-Solo.png|thumb|left|300px|Blawz and Crodit during the revolt on Kessel.]]
By [[10 BBY]],<ref name="10 BBY">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' featuring [[Blawz]] and [[Crodit]] to [[10 BBY]].</ref> the Dwuni brothers [[Blawz]] and [[Crodit]] were [[Slavery|enslaved]] [[Miner|workers]] in the extensive [[Spice mines of Kessel|mines]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Kessel]]<ref name="SoloGuide" /> who had been brought there from off-world.<ref name="GeneralEquipment">{{EncyclopediaCite|General Equipment (2)}}</ref> Under the supervision of the [[Pyke Syndicate]] and the [[Mining Guild]], the [[Mining|mines]] were worked by [[prisoner]]s who had generally been captured by the [[Galactic Empire]]. Equipped with [[portable drill unit]]s and back-mounted pneumatic [[compressor]] packs, Blawz and Crodit used their small body size to squeeze into otherwise inaccessible areas of the mines&mdash;work that, unusually, the pair enjoyed.<ref name="SoloGuide" /> That [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="10 BBY" /> the [[pilot droid]] [[L3-37]] began a [[Raid on Kessel|revolt]] among the [[droid]] workforce of the mines' operations center as part of a heist she and her [[Beckett's gang|companions]] were carrying out there, which in turn led to the liberation of the enslaved miners. Afterward, Blawz and Crodit were among the workers who rushed out of the mines and onto the planet's surface.<ref name="Solo" />

[[File:Dwuni-Reckoning.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Three Dwuni (pictured) were scared out of their shuttered store during a Pre-Mor Authority operation on Ferrix.]]
A trio of [[Clothing|uniformed]] Dwuni worked at a store in [[Ferrix City]] on<ref name="Reckoning" /> the Outer Rim world<ref name="DoR">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> [[Ferrix]]<ref name="Reckoning" /> in [[5 BBY]].<ref name="5 BBY">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]'' dates the events of "[[Reckoning (episode)|Reckoning]]" to [[5 BBY]].</ref> When a team of [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Pre-Mor Authority]] [[Pre-Mor Authority Security Forces|security forces]] [[Tac-Corpo|troopers]] under the [[Commanding officer|command]] of the human<ref name="Reckoning" /> [[Deputy Inspector]]<ref name="ReckoningEpGuide2">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e3-story-gallery|text="Reckoning" Story Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 2}}</ref> [[Syril Karn]] arrived in the [[city]] in order to [[Ambush on Ferrix|arrest]] the [[Ferrixian]] human [[thief]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], in response the local citizens started making coordinated noise using [[metal]] implements<ref name="Reckoning" /> in order to warn the fugitive.<ref name="ReckoningEpGuide5">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e3-story-gallery|text="Reckoning" Story Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 5}}</ref> The local shops also shuttered, with the three Dwuni hiding at their place of business.<ref name="Reckoning" />

Karn later entered the store while attempting to set up an ambush for Andor and, inside the premises, tried to hail any potential occupants. The Dwuni attempted to slip out through a back door unnoticed, though the startled [[officer]] shot his [[blaster pistol]] at the [[alien]]s when he noticed them, causing the agitated trio to yelp out and then chatter among themselves while they made their escape. Afterward, the three panting Dwuni were running through a narrow street where they were noticed by Andor and his contact, the [[Axis network]] leader [[Luthen Rael]], with the two humans subsequently ambushing the still-waiting Karn at the store.<ref name="Reckoning" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Dwuni first appeared in the [[2018]] ''[[Star Wars Anthology Series]]'' film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Solo" /> The species was first identified by [[Pablo Hidalgo]]'s accompanying reference book ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''.<ref name="SoloGuide" />

